WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.472 --> 00:00:08.775
Everything so far runs in your browser alone. This last part only exists where a deployment has sign-in.

2
00:00:13.576 --> 00:00:26.749
And a note before it does: the sailors on these boards are invented. A machine shooting a film has no server with real players on it. The tab, the digest and the ranking are the app's own.

3
00:00:26.749 --> 00:00:31.724
Sixteen boards, built from the sailors who chose to stand on them.

4
00:00:35.926 --> 00:00:40.120
A place on a board is a door. This is that sailor's card:

5
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.028
their fleet, their crew, and what they have done at sea.

6
00:00:48.959 --> 00:00:53.088
And this is their ship, on your own Ship tab, fully fitted.

7
00:00:53.088 --> 00:00:57.892
To look at, and not to keep. One press puts you back on yours.

8
00:01:09.842 --> 00:01:13.793
The other half of the tab adds the whole fleet up.

9
00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:17.244
Nothing goes onto a board that was not offered.

10
00:01:17.244 --> 00:01:22.467
You see the exact digest before you agree to it, and leaving deletes it again.

11
00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:32.818
Your data stays in your browser. You sign in to sync it between machines, or to take part in this. Neither is required to use anything else.
